A(('p', '13.3 Final Synthesis. Jesus tells Simon of a certain creditor who had two debtors, five hundred pence and fifty, who had nothing to pay and were both frankly forgiven. He asks which will love him most, and Simon answers “he, to whom he forgave most.” Jesus says he has rightly judged, then sets what Simon did not give beside what the woman did, and says what He says about her sins, her love and the one forgiven little. He names nothing else in the story.'))
