A(('call', 'Boundaries to Remember',
   'Jesus names what Simon did not give, what the woman did, her sins forgiven and the one forgiven little, and nothing more. No identity for the creditor, the debtors or the pence. No symbol carried in from another parable. Forgiving, loving and believing are actions in a story and a scene, not steps of salvation. The Body of Christ is neither the debtor nor the woman. The lessons are principles of conduct, not a transfer of Kingdom identity to the Body.'))

